{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"edible-insane-mongrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nOn `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`, `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md:72-74` describes a bare `pip install .[agents,reviewbot]`, while `infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot` uses the locked uv install with `agents,reviewbot,bedrock`. Lines 211-215 describe two compose containers, but the stack now runs Gerrit, review-bot, opcert, and MCP; nginx remains host-side. This gives operators a stale dependency and topology model.\n\n## Approach\nUpdate the operator guide to match the current Dockerfile and compose topology. Leave historical ADR text unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The review-bot installation description matches the locked uv command and current extras in `Dockerfile.reviewbot`.\n- [ ] The deployment topology names all four compose services and distinguishes host-side nginx.\n- [ ] Historical ADR 0007 remains unchanged.\n- [ ] Documentation checks and `make lint` pass.","id":"1d89-2206-bb64-4d98","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["documentation","gerrit","infra","drift"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Update Gerrit AWS setup for locked review-bot install and four-service stack"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788594869468850001,"uuid":"9edda117-e7b6-4805-9e34-cb418295d29a"}